\strong{Cruise events.} A dataset's root samples carry \code{cruise_key} but no parent, so
\code{cruises = TRUE} (the default) emits one event per cruise the dataset touches and
parents the roots to it. That is a derivation from a column already on the row,
not an invention, and it is what makes an archive's events group the way a reader
expects. \code{cruises = FALSE} leaves the roots parentless.

Nothing here asserts \code{countryCode}, \code{waterBody} or \code{coordinateUncertaintyInMeters}:
the release measures none of them, and the ichthyo notebook's hand-typed values
were dataset metadata living where no provider could edit them (D-8).
